    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The suite is green. Here's what I changed to make `householdId` deterministic and implement the new household semantics.\n\n## Core change: deterministic `householdId`\n- **`OwnerIdentity.householdIdFor`** now derives the id from `(lastName, postcode)` instead of `(lastName, address)`: the first **12** hex chars of `SHA-256(normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode)`. Returns `null` when there's no postcode (an owner without a postcode is in no household).\n- **`AssignHousehold`** now *always* stamps this deterministic id (dropped the `sharesHousehold` gate and the loop that stamped other owners) \u2014 owners with the same last name and postcode share it automatically.\n\n## `sharesHousehold` now only bypasses the duplicate block\n- **`CheckIdentityUnique`** enforces two rules, both keyed off the computed household:\n  1. **Exact identity duplicate** (same telephone+email+household) \u2192 always 409.\n  2. **Household duplicate** \u2014 the new owner's computed `householdId` matches an existing owner's (i.e. same last name + postcode) \u2192 409 **unless** the request sets `sharesHousehold: true`, which bypasses it and creates a declared member.\n\n## Declared members aren't suspected duplicates\n- **`PossibleDuplicate.sharesHousehold`** (new helper) + both responders (`RespondWithOwnerCreated`, `RespondWithOwner`) suppress the `possibleDuplicate` flag for any owner sharing its `householdId` with another owner. This is consistent across the create response and later GETs (which have no request flag to read).\n\n## Household-size input to the membership level\n- **`MembershipLevel.of(owner, repo)`** now adds its second point when the owner is the **sole member of their household at creation** (no *earlier* owner shares the computed `householdId`; no-postcode owners are always sole) \u2014 replacing the old `namesakeCount == 0` bump. Only lower-id owners count, so the level stays fixed at creation even as the household grows.\n- Wired through **`OwnerMapper`** (injected `OwnerRepository`, `membershipLevel(owner)` helper used by the mapping expression) so create, GET, and list responses agree, and **`AuditOwnerCreated`** logs the same value. The audit log during the test run confirms it: the declared member logged `membershipLevel=2\u21921` relative to sole members.\n\nI also updated the OpenAPI descriptions (`sharesHousehold`, `householdId`, `membershipLevel`, `possibleDuplicate`) to match the new behaviour.\n\n`namesakeCount` itself (the separately-documented first+last-name count) is untouched. The existing acceptance test and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`), and temporary tests I ran and then removed confirmed the 409-on-second-same-household, the `sharesHousehold` bypass with no duplicate flag, and that a differing postcode is a different household.",
